msgid "``em.plugins`` — plugins loaded from disk"
msgstr ""

msgid "Generated for em API |api| from the docstrings of :mod:`s3dgraphy.em.plugins`."
msgstr ""

msgid "The plugins loaded from disk — W14 of the extensions plan (MICRO-PL17, E.D. 18 Nov 2026)."
msgstr ""

msgid "A plugin is the ``[code]`` section of an ``em-extension.toml`` (a pure plugin, or the code of a mixed package), installed by :mod:`s3dgraphy.extensions` (W21) under ``~/.s3dgraphy/plugins/<source>/<id>/<code version>/`` with its ``.install.json``, and made active per host in ``enabled.json``. This module LOADS what is active, in the host's Python (SPEC-plugin §3.2):"
msgstr ""

msgid "**discovery** — :func:`sync` reads ``active_code(host)``;"
msgstr ""

msgid "**checks without running** — the folder is there; ``em_api_min``/``max`` against :data:`s3dgraphy.em.API_VERSION` (§14.7); the wheels' Python against this interpreter; the descriptor holds; the module does not hide one of the program's (a plugin called ``json``);"
msgstr ""

msgid "**activation** — the folder (and its wheels) on ``sys.path``, the module imported, ``setup(ctx)`` called: it wires the declared commands (``ctx.command``), listens (``ctx.on``), exposes functions to the console (``ctx.expose``);"
msgstr ""

msgid "**use** — every command passes the contract's ``invoke`` (the four refusals: unknown, declared and not wired, a slot missing, a write with no author); inside it, ``em.write`` writes AS THE PLUGIN — its declared capabilities are the seam's (``guard_write``), a command declared ``writes = false`` cannot write at all; a handler that raises is caught and said, the host stays up;"
msgstr ""

msgid "**deactivation** — ``teardown(ctx)``, its listeners and handlers off. The module stays in ``sys.modules`` (§3.2: not promised in 1.6): another VERSION of the same plugin needs the host to restart, and says so."
msgstr ""

msgid "A command IS a :class:`~s3dgraphy.contract.Descriptor` (``name`` = ``<plugin>/<command>``, ``input_schema`` = its slots, ``writes``), registered in a :class:`~s3dgraphy.contract.Registry`. Where it is drawn is the host's: the manifest's ``in`` names the slots (:mod:`s3dgraphy.extensions.slots`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "``ctx.package`` is the data of the same envelope (a mixed package: the package's version the code came with), ``None`` for a pure plugin (§17.4)."
msgstr ""

msgid "MICRO-PL25 (row X5 of the plan) · the slots of phase 2. A command may also be drawn in ``inspector.section@1``, ``tabular.column@1``, ``statusbar@1`` (it only reads: :func:`compute` runs many at once and gives back their values in the shape the host draws, :func:`shape`) and ``space.tool@1`` (its ``primitive`` and ``icon``; the host fills its ``geometry`` slot with what the person placed). ``[[code.panels]]`` are the declarative panels (``panel@1``): :class:`PanelDecl`, fields the host draws, values computed by read-only commands, buttons that invoke commands."
msgstr ""

msgid "MICRO-GEO11 (row G10 of the geophysics plan) · ``space.layer@1``: a read-only command (``layer = \"raster_stack\"``) describes a layer of the Space — planes with a picture in a frame of their own — and the host draws it; :func:`shape` gives the one description a host reads (:func:`_shape_layer`), the pictures named by a path INSIDE the plugin's own data folder (``plugins-data/<id>/``), the only place a host serves them from."
msgstr ""

