msgstr ""

msgid "``em.ext`` — what the loaded plugins expose to the console (``em.ext.facemesh_fit.propose``; ``em.ext[\"esempio-statuaria\"]`` for an id that is not a Python name: ``-`` reads as ``_`` too)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The plugin (and command) on whose behalf ``em.write`` is writing, or None."
msgstr ""

msgid "Load what is active for ``host`` and not loaded; unload what is no longer active; a version changed needs a restart (said). Cheap: one read of ``enabled.json``. Returns the plugins, in id order."
msgstr ""

msgid "``dev`` (W15a): the plugins of the development folder (:func:`s3dgraphy.extensions.dev_dir`) count too, loaded where they are, with no installation and no trust question — the HOST says when (EMStudio: «Funzioni sperimentali» on). A development copy hides an installed plugin with the same id, and says so. ``dev=False`` unloads them."
msgstr ""

msgid "Every plugin known to this process (whatever its state), by id."
msgstr ""

msgid "The plugin ``pid`` known to this process, or None."
msgstr ""

msgid "``teardown(ctx)``; the listeners, handlers and exposed functions off. The module stays imported (§3.2)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Every plugin off (tests; a host closing)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The declared commands of the plugins of this process (``slot``: only those drawn there, ``\"context.node\"`` or ``\"context.node@1\"``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Everything a host draws: the plugins (state, problems in EN and IT, commands with their slots), and how many listeners per event."
msgstr ""

msgid "Every declared command as a Descriptor (wired or not)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The command as the contract sees it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Run a plugin's command through the contract. ``result.data``: ``reason`` (a refusal's name), ``messages`` (EN, IT), ``value`` (what the handler returned, when JSON can say it), ``file`` (an exporter's)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Every ``check@1`` command of the loaded plugins, read-only: the warnings they return (``{rule, sev, node, txt}``), each with its plugin; a check that fails or returns something else is ONE warning that says so."
msgstr ""

msgid "The readers of «Porta dentro…» (``door.reader``) for this file or folder."
msgstr ""

msgid "A file: those that ACCEPT it by its extension (taken from the host); with ``claimed=True`` those that only CLAIM it (``door.reader@2``: offered as «Read as: …» beside the host's own reading, never taken). A folder (``is_dir``; None = ask the disk): the ``@2`` readers with ``folders = true``."
msgstr ""

msgid "The commands of a ``[code]`` section; a command with an entry the host cannot draw keeps the others (§14.7: the entry, not the plugin)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The folder of the plugins' own state, kept across updates: ``S3DGRAPHY_PLUGINS_DATA_DIR``, else ``~/.s3dgraphy/plugins-data``."
msgstr ""

msgid "the folder of a plugin's own state, kept across updates (SPEC-plugin §14.3)"
msgstr ""

msgid "``[[code.panels]]``, read (``panel@1``, MICRO-PL25): a declarative panel — the host draws its fields; nothing of the plugin runs in the page."
msgstr ""

msgid "The panel's full name, ``<plugin>/<panel>``."
msgstr ""

msgid "The panels of a ``[code]`` section; a field that does not read is left out (the validator said it), a field that names a command the plugin does not declare too."
msgstr ""

msgid "What a host draws of a read-only command's ``value`` in ``slot``:"
msgstr ""

msgid "``statusbar`` — one line of text (≤ :data:`STATUS_MAX`);"
msgstr ""

msgid "``tabular.column`` — ``{id: text}`` (each ≤ :data:`CELL_MAX`);"
msgstr ""

msgid "``inspector.section`` and a panel's ``value`` — rows ``[{label, value}]`` (≤ :data:`ROWS_MAX`) from a dict (label → value), a list of ``{label, value}`` or of pairs, or a text (one row without a label);"
msgstr ""

msgid "``space.layer`` (MICRO-GEO11) — a list of layers (≤ :data:`LAYERS_MAX`) from a layer or a list of layers, each as :func:`_shape_layer` gives it."
msgstr ""

msgid "``(False, None)`` when the value has another shape (said by the caller)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The values of phase 2 at once: each item ``{key, plugin, command, slot, slots}`` is a READ-ONLY command (``writes = false``; one that is not is refused before it runs, one that tries to write is refused by the seam) run through the contract; the answer per item ``{key, ok, value}`` (in the shape of :func:`shape`) or ``{key, ok: false, messages: {en, it}}``. At most :data:`COMPUTE_MAX` items; one that fails never stops the others."
msgstr ""

